cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "lex-corpus-lu-legilux, verbatim consolidated Luxembourg law"
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite it, and cite Legilux as the source of the texts."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Hajji
    given-names: Soufien
repository-code: "https://github.com/SFHAJJI/lex-corpus-lu-legilux"
url: "https://law.soufien.lu"
abstract: >-
  Every consolidated version of Luxembourg law that Legilux publishes, stored as the
  publisher's own bytes with no reformatting, plus dated JSON metadata carrying the
  publisher-asserted validity interval, an append-only observation chain, and a SHA-256 over
  the record itself. Append-only: the repository only ever gains commits. The tree is laid
  out by work and validity date, so it reads as a legislative history; the commit log is an
  ingest log, and the two are deliberately not the same.
keywords:
  - legal-data
  - legislation
  - luxembourg
  - consolidated-legislation
  - point-in-time
  - open-data
  - akoma-ntoso
license: CC-BY-4.0
